WHO   — THE RNA WORLD — a life-science sphere — the brainless mind
WHAT  — Before DNA, before proteins, before cells — a single kind of molecule may have done it all. RNA can carry information like a gene and speed reactions like an enzyme, so it can copy itself with no help. The RNA world is the leading guess at life's first chapter: the moment chemistry learned to reproduce, and began.
WHERE — intelligence without a brain  Framework inputs: the living; the rule; the signal; the open question  Conductor / external anchor: ROOT0 (catalogued into UD0)
